// The subscriber's side (business book §4.3, §4.5, §6.1, §10, §14.1, §14.5):
// the demo's listeners, a student verification by the simulated provider, a
// quote confirmed into a subscription with a simulated payment, and the
// account a listener sees.
//
// Who the subscriber is: every request names subscriber_id, which the gateway
// takes from the site's session (a demo listener chosen at the entrance) and
// never from a field the browser filled, as for GetQuoteRequest. These calls
// carry no x-actor: in the audit log their author is the subscriber, with the
// role "subscriber". VerifyStudent and ConfirmQuote change something and carry
// an idempotency-key.
//
// Nothing here moves money or checks a real student record: the payment
// provider and the student verifier are simulated stand-ins behind small
// interfaces, they say so in every answer, and a real provider would plug in
// there.

